ensation occurs \(N140\) and the evaluation of the sensation \(P300\) both have significant effects on temporal neural activity. Throughout the entirety of the post stimulus SEP, the sine waveform exhibited the highest neural amplitude, closely followed b\
y square. This likely is caused by the high combination of intensity and area that both of these waveforms were able to evoke compared to the three triangular waveforms.)/K 6/P 25 0 R/Pg 1105 0 R/S/Figure>>
